---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DarkHeader from '../../components/DarkHeader.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Trail / Range: what MPG costs you off-road — Cooper Minehart"
  description="40 stock vehicles scored on off-road geometry and plotted against EPA fuel economy. Which ones nobody beats on both."
>
  <DarkHeader>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-10">
      <a href="/hobbies" class="text-sm text-forest-400 hover:text-forest-300 mb-6 inline-block">← Hobbies</a>
      <p class="section-label-light mb-3">Hobbies · Trail / Range</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-3">What MPG costs you off-road</h1>
      <p class="text-stone-300 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        40 stock vehicles, scored on geometry and plotted against fuel economy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </DarkHeader>

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-10 pb-24 text-[#1a1a1a]">
    <div class="space-y-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#333]">
      <p>
        TLDR; I wanted to know how much fuel economy you give up to get something that can actually
        go off road. Of 31 gas and hybrid vehicles, 9 aren't beaten on both capability and MPG. The
        2024 Tacoma TRD Pro hybrid is where the curve bends (23 mpg, score 62). Add EVs and only the
        two Broncos stay on the frontier, an R1S scores within 2 points of the Sasquatch at $9.64 per
        100 miles (Sasquatch $26.05, Pittsburgh prices).
      </p>
      <p>
        The score is 0-100 and only looks at static geometry: ground clearance (30%), approach,
        departure and breakover angles (20% each) and tire diameter (10%), each scaled between fixed
        endpoints (clearance 6 to 13 in, etc). Lockers and low range are filters, not points. MPG is
        EPA combined. Every chart below is live, hover a point or click the buttons.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] pt-4">
        9 vehicles nobody beats on both, the top end is steep
      </h2>
    </div>

    <figure class="tr-fig" data-tr-fig="field">
      <div class="tr-chips" aria-label="Required hardware"></div>
      <div class="tr-wrap"><svg role="img" aria-label="Off-road score vs EPA combined MPG, gas and hybrid vehicles"></svg><div class="tr-tip" hidden></div></div>
      <figcaption class="tr-live"></figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#333]">
      <p>
        On the frontier means nothing else scores as well on both axes and better on one. Going from
        the Bronco Raptor (15 mpg, 92) to a 2-door Sasquatch (18 mpg, 78) costs 14 points for 3 mpg.
        Below the Tacoma it flips, the next 16 mpg (RAV4 hybrid, 39) costs 39 points. The RAV4
        Woodland scores 0.1 better than the LE for 2 mpg less (couldn't find Toyota's breakover so
        both are estimated).
      </p>
      <p>
        Click "Low range only" and the frontier is 4: Raptor, Sasquatch, Rubicon 2-door, Tacoma.
        Nothing with a low range transfer case here gets more than 23 mpg.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] pt-4">
        2-doors beat 4-doors, the 4Runner and Land Cruiser aren't close
      </h2>
      <p>
        Wheelbase shows up through breakover. The 4-door Rubicon loses 5° of breakover to the 2-door
        (22.6° vs 27.8°) and gets 1 mpg worse. The 2015 4Runner Trail scores 46 at 18 mpg, the
        Sasquatch scores 78 at the same 18. The 2024 Land Cruiser scores 43 at 23 mpg with the same
        2.4L hybrid as the Tacoma TRD Pro, which scores 62. Closest miss is a 2-door Wrangler Sport,
        0.4 points behind the Tacoma at the same 23 mpg.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] pt-4">
        Add EVs and only the Broncos survive
      </h2>
      <p>
        MPGe doesn't compare at the pump, so this axis is energy cost per 100 miles (gas: 100 ÷ mpg ×
        $/gal, EV: EPA kWh/100 mi × $/kWh). The order holds at all 5 city prices, even Honolulu at
        $0.48/kWh. The R1S breakover is estimated.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="tr-fig" data-tr-fig="ev">
      <div class="tr-chips" aria-label="Energy prices"></div>
      <div class="tr-wrap"><svg role="img" aria-label="Off-road score vs energy cost per 100 miles, all 40 vehicles"></svg><div class="tr-tip" hidden></div></div>
      <figcaption class="tr-live"></figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#333]">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a] pt-4">
        Weights move the Tacoma, not the Crosstrek
      </h2>
      <p>
        7 vehicles make the frontier under all 4 presets: Sasquatch 2-door, Rubicon 2-door, Renegade
        Trailhawk, both Crosstreks and both RAV4 hybrids. The Tacoma only makes it when clearance
        counts most, weight the angles or a short wheelbase and the 2-door Wrangler Sport takes its
        spot. Short wheelbase drops the Raptor (116.5 in).
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="tr-fig" data-tr-fig="weights">
      <div class="tr-chips" aria-label="Weight preset"></div>
      <div class="tr-wrap"><svg role="img" aria-label="Frontier under different score weights"></svg><div class="tr-tip" hidden></div></div>
      <figcaption class="tr-live"></figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#333]">
      <p>
        What it doesn't capture: traction, articulation, gearing, armor, reliability, price. EPA
        combined is a lab number and manufacturers measure clearance differently. 40 configurations
        (2010-2027) is a curated list, not every trim. Tell me what's missing.
      </p>
      <p>Set your own weights, filters and gas prices below.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-8">
      <div class="border border-stone-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-white shadow-sm">
        <iframe
          src="/maps/trail-range/index.html"
          title="Trail / Range off-road vs fuel economy explorer"
          class="w-full block"
          style="height: 90vh; min-height: 760px; border: 0;"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption class="text-xs text-[#888] mt-3 text-center">
        Trail / Range. Sources and EPA records for every point are in the tool. Specs reviewed Oct 2, 2026.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-stone-200 text-sm text-[#555] leading-relaxed">
      <p>Cooper Minehart</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <script is:inline src="/maps/trail-range/model.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="/maps/trail-range/data.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="/maps/trail-range/post-charts.js"></script>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .tr-fig { margin: 1.75rem 0 2rem; }
  .tr-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem; margin-bottom: .6rem; }
  .tr-chip { font-size: 12.5px; padding: .3rem .7rem; border: 1px solid #d6d3cc; border-radius: 999px; background: #fff; color: #444; cursor: pointer; }
  .tr-chip[aria-pressed="true"] { background: #172d30; border-color: #172d30; color: #fff; }
  .tr-wrap { position: relative; border: 1px solid #e7e5e0; border-radius: 8px; background: #fffefa; }
  .tr-wrap svg { display: block; width: 100%; }
  .tr-ax { font-size: 11px; fill: #626e6c; }
  .tr-axt { font-size: 11.5px; fill: #172d30; }
  .tr-lab { fill: #626e6c; }
  .tr-on { fill: #172d30; font-weight: 600; }
  .tr-pt { cursor: pointer; }
  .tr-tip { position: absolute; pointer-events: none; background: #172d30; color: #fff; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.4; padding: .45rem .6rem; border-radius: 6px; max-width: 220px; z-index: 5; }
  .tr-live { font-size: 12px; color: #888; margin-top: .5rem; line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
